---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Label from "../components/Label.astro";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../schema";
import { ORG, CONTACT, SUBPROCESSORS, LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE } from "../consts";

const schemas = [
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Privacy Policy", path: "/privacy-policy" },
  ]),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Website Support Studio collects, uses, protects, and shares information across the public site, checkout, customer accounts, and support portal."
  path="/privacy-policy"
  schemas={schemas}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="prose">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span><Label text="privacy_policy" /></span>
      </nav>
      <p class="kicker"><Label text="_legal" /></p>
      <h1><Label text="privacy_policy" /></h1>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted);">Effective {LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

      <div class="summary" style="margin:1.5rem 0;">
        <strong>Summary.</strong> Website Support Studio is operated by {ORG.legalName}. We collect the
        information needed to respond to inquiries, process checkout, authenticate users, onboard customer
        websites, receive website requests, store request attachments, and operate the customer/operator
        portal. We do not sell personal information.
      </div>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Website Support Studio ("WSS", "we", "us") is operated by {ORG.legalName}, organized in the
        {ORG.jurisdiction}. Our principal place of business is in {ORG.address.locality}, {ORG.address.region}.
        For questions, contact <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Services covered</h2>
      <p>
        This policy covers the public marketing website at websitesupportstudio.com, the customer/operator
        app at app.websitesupportstudio.com, checkout and onboarding flows, and the support workflows used
        to deliver Website Support Studio services. Third-party sites we link to have their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Information we collect</h2>
      <h3>Information you provide</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Contact information</strong> such as your name, email address, company, message content, and booking details when you email us, book a call, or request information.</li>
        <li><strong>Checkout information</strong> handled by Stripe, including buyer email, customer/payment identifiers, plan, subscription status, and billing period information returned to WSS through Stripe webhooks.</li>
        <li><strong>Account information</strong> from Supabase Auth, including authenticated user ID, email address, OAuth provider/session data, and account state.</li>
        <li><strong>Onboarding information</strong> including company name, website URL, website count, CMS/platform, primary contact name, primary contact email, and support email.</li>
        <li><strong>Website request information</strong> including site, title, description, priority, request status, ticket number, submitter email, messages, approvals, audit events, and related workflow records.</li>
        <li><strong>Attachments</strong> you upload to a request, including file name, file type, file size, storage path, and the file contents. Uploaded attachments may be retrievable through Supabase Storage public URLs used by the portal.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Analytics information.</strong> The public marketing site currently uses Google Analytics 4 when configured. Analytics may collect pages viewed, referral source, approximate location derived from IP address, device/browser information, and interaction events. GA4 is configured with IP anonymization.</li>
        <li><strong>Operational logs.</strong> Vercel, Supabase, Stripe, and other service providers may process IP address, request metadata, timestamps, error logs, and security events needed to host, secure, debug, and operate the service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to inquiries, book calls, scope work, and provide support.</li>
        <li>To process checkout, maintain subscription/payment status, and provision customer workspaces.</li>
        <li>To authenticate users and route customers/operators to the correct workspace.</li>
        <li>To complete onboarding, create site records, receive website requests, and track project status.</li>
        <li>To store request attachments and maintain request history, approvals, and audit trails.</li>
        <li>To measure and improve the public website and service experience.</li>
        <li>To protect the service, prevent abuse, comply with legal obligations, and enforce agreements.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        The public marketing site currently uses Google Analytics 4 when configured. The app uses Supabase
        Auth browser session storage when real login is enabled. We do not use advertising, retargeting, or
        cross-site marketing pixels in the current implementation. See the <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>
        for more detail.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Communications</h2>
      <p>
        We may use your email address to respond to inquiries, send checkout or account-related messages,
        communicate about requests, and provide service notices. Marketing emails, if introduced, will
        include an appropriate way to opt out.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Third-party providers</h2>
      <p>
        We use service providers to operate WSS. They process information only for the services they provide
        to us. Current providers reflected in the implementation include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        {SUBPROCESSORS.map((s) => <li><strong>{s.name}</strong> — {s.role} ({s.region}).</li>)}
        <li><strong>Google Calendar</strong> — appointment booking links.</li>
        <li><strong>LinkedIn</strong> — outbound company profile link.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain personal information for as long as needed to provide the service, maintain customer and
        audit records, comply with legal/tax obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce agreements. Request
        history, approvals, and audit records may be retained as part of the service accountability model.
        When information is no longer needed, we delete or anonymize it where practical.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use technical and organizational safeguards such as authenticated access, role-aware routing,
        tenant-scoped Supabase policies/RPCs, service-role separation for server functions, request audit
        records, and Vercel security headers. No internet service can be guaranteed completely secure.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, or receive a
        copy of your personal information, or to object to certain processing. We do not sell personal
        information. To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>. We may
        need to verify your identity before responding.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Children</h2>
      <p>Website Support Studio is a business service and is not directed to children under 16.</p>

      <h2>12. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the service changes. The effective date above will be updated when the
        policy changes materially.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
